  "details": "I personally remember the names of most of my world and avatar favorites. It would be nice to be able to just quick search my favorites for what I'm looking for instead of needing to scroll lists. Currently my best solution is to sort alphabetically but that still entails searching because I never know which of my six avatar categories the avatar I'm looking for is in.\n\n(Honestly if I could control it I would just smush all my VRC+ favorites into one big category because then sorting would work better. I understand the need to have a separate category for non-VRC+ favorites because you want to be able to know which avatars will become unavailable if your subscription ends. But currently we have to spread our favorites across 6 different categories and most of my time searching for an avatar is spent trying to remember which category it's in).\n\nYou've already added a search function for settings, so maybe it would be nice to expand that to avatars and world favorites too. Maybe the social menu too, surely it's faster and easier on the servers to search your personal lists than it is to search all of VRChat? The website already has a search for friends and I find it odd that the client doesn't have that too. Sometimes people just want to find the profile of a specific offline friend.\n\nThanks.",
